# wgq: only dom0 makes and dresses qubes.
#
# Everything below restates the Admin API's own default: no VM may
# create a qube, clone one, or change which label a qube wears. What
# this file adds is permanence, the same way 30-wgq-labels.policy pins
# the label namespace: sorted at 30, these denies keep matching first
# even if a management qube is someday granted broad admin.* powers by
# a later-sorted allow.
#
# A qube's NAME cannot be pinned by policy at all: it travels in the
# call's payload, and policy sees only service, argument, source and
# destination. That is fine -- a name is a string, while the label is
# the identity Qubes actually draws (border colour, icon), and with
# this file both minting qubes and dressing them stay dom0's alone,
# permanently. dom0 itself is not subject to policy, which is the
# point.
#
# admin.vm.CreateDisposable is deliberately absent: its qubes are
# auto-named disp#### and inherit their template's label, so it can
# impersonate nothing -- and denying it could break disposable flows.
admin.vm.Create.AppVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.Create.DispVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.Create.StandaloneVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.Create.TemplateVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.CreateInPool.AppVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.CreateInPool.DispVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.CreateInPool.StandaloneVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.CreateInPool.TemplateVM * * @adminvm deny notify=yes
admin.vm.Clone * * * deny notify=yes
admin.vm.property.Set +label * * deny notify=yes
admin.vm.property.Reset +label * * deny notify=yes
